DISTILLED 2026-08-18 after read-only Codex-xhigh, Opus-xhigh and Tau reviews. The old ~30.8 KiB umbrella is not an rb-lite input. It is now six bounded children:
1. btc-policy-mby-manifest-v1-zero-ceiling-88w — 800 gross Rust;
2. btc-policy-mby-operator-core-signer-7vb — 900;
3. btc-policy-mby-spend-composer-l5p — 500;
4. btc-policy-mby-spend-command-6mp — 500;
5. btc-policy-mby-escape-command-role-swap-8bt — 850;
6. btc-policy-mby-seal-to-operate-e2e-mmo — 500.
Gross means additions plus deletions and EVERY test line is included. Total 4,050 Rust = about 1,450 production + 2,600 tests (64.2% tests), plus 700 non-Rust lines. The older 2,500–4,500 estimate did not say whether tests/deletions were included and is superseded.

Occam decisions: one parse-only legacy DTO with no v0 hash/live dispatch; relay client and spending signer land together but remain separate types/credentials; one stable Core composer; one normal command; one known-outpoint escape command; one stage-1 artifact-to-command E2E. Escape is explicitly : pending IDs disclose no coins, residual is every other stable confirmed vault UTXO, one-UTXO/all-selected cases fail before signing, and the runbook must say not to guess. No pending API expansion or automatic reserve gamble. M1 may land first as repository code, but NO production ceremony/deployment is authorized while mby remains open.

Hidden serialization: btc-policy-5ag follows M1 and owns the next version bump for its manifest network field; M2 follows both so the live parser is written once against sealed network state. wdu follows M1+5ag; sqn follows M4. Other complete-product dependents remain on this umbrella. Exact child descriptions, not this summary, are implementation authority.
